
DOORS
=====

There  are  some commands that are executable from MTalk, but they are
not built into MTalk.  These door commands typically call external DOS
commands or utilities.  To the user, doors are entered and executed in
the  same  manner as internal commands.  The number and types of doors
configured  varies from system to system.  When you are using MTalk in
text  windowing  mode  (by executing /WIN OPEN) you may experience the
garbling  of  your  screen  after  you  execute a door command.  If it
should happen, you must press control-L to redraw the screen.

